<title>USA: Western Pacific to buy six Boeing jets.</title>
<headline>Western Pacific to buy six Boeing jets.</headline>
<dateline>COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Pacific Airlines said Wednesday it will buy six new Boeing 737-300s in 1997 with an option to buy six Boeing 737-700s in 1998 and beyond.</p>
<p>The company did not disclose how much it was paying for the aircraft and did not immediately respond to inquiries.</p>
<p>The aircraft are to be delivered between May and December 1997.  </p>
<p>Western Pacific would not disclose the price of the order. However, Boeing Corp's commercial airplane division said the 737-300s ordered are worth $246 million.</p>
</text>
